Skip TIPC source compilation in libzmq to match upstream's archive.

GUIX builds bitcoin via a cross-toolchain (`make-bitcoin-cross-toolchain`
in contrib/guix/manifest.scm) so CMake sees `CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING=ON`
when libzmq configures. libzmq's CMakeLists.txt wraps the runtime
TIPC check in `if(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)` and only adds the three
TIPC source files when `ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC` is set:

  if(NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
    ...
    zmq_check_tcp_tipc()   # sets ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC=1 if test runs OK
  endif()
  ...
  if(ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC)
    list(APPEND cxx-sources tipc_address.cpp tipc_connecter.cpp tipc_listener.cpp)
  endif()

Under GUIX's cross-compile, the check is skipped → ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC stays
undefined → no TIPC sources → upstream's libzmq.a excludes them
(verified by ar-extracting upstream's depends staging archive).

We build natively, so the check runs, succeeds (linux/tipc.h plus a
working PF_TIPC kernel in the Nix sandbox), and our libzmq.a ends up
with three extra objects: tipc_address.cpp.o, tipc_connecter.cpp.o,
tipc_listener.cpp.o — adding ~44 KiB to libzmq.a and ~4-5 KiB of
.text in the final bitcoind.

Pin `ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC` to FALSE just before the conditional so it
matches GUIX's behavior regardless of CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING.

This patch is applied to the libzmq 4.3.5 source tree inside Bitcoin
Core's depends/sources, before the depends Makefile runs its own
patches.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1208,6 +1208,7 @@
   list(APPEND cxx-sources vmci_address.cpp vmci_connecter.cpp vmci_listener.cpp vmci.cpp)
 endif()

+set(ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC FALSE)
 if(ZMQ_HAVE_TIPC)
   list(APPEND cxx-sources tipc_address.cpp tipc_connecter.cpp tipc_listener.cpp)
 endif()
